  "security_implications": "The select signals (data_in_prev_sel_o, state_in_sel_o, add_state_in_sel_o, add_state_out_sel_o, key_init_sel_o, iv_sel_o) control multiplexing of AES internal state, data paths, key memory, and IV registers. Faulty OR combination (due to mismatch) may lead to unauthorized access to key material or use of wrong key/IV state. The error flag mr_err does not gate these outputs; any transient or permanent fault can propagate a dangerous select before the system reacts, potentially leaking secret or corrupting secure state. The design assumes a downstream consumer will handle the mr_err and disable affected data paths, but no local containment is implemented.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "aes_control.sv:474-502"
  ],
